Things you will need:
1 Onion
3-4 Habanero (your choice)
Goat meat (As many as you need)
1 Pot
Chopping board
water
crushed chill pepper
pepper soup spice (Seasoning)
ginger (Seasoning)
Salt (Seasoning)
Maggi (chicken boullion seasoning)
Garlic (Seasoning)
Thyme (Seasoning)

Please use the 1/2 teaspoon measurement for everything:
Taste is key - you must taste it as you add the ingredients
Texture is up to you, depending on how soft you like the meat
Please wash the meat before cooking 

Instructions for making it:
First, you cut up the meat into the size you want or like. If it's already the size you want, put it in the pot
Then you chop up the habanero peppers (the amount you use is up to you)
Then you dice up one onion
Add water to the pot with onion, pepper, and meat
Put the pot on fire, and while you are boiling it, add;

1/2 teaspoon of the following:
Salt with a little extra, barely 2 spoons
Thyme
Ginger
Garlic
Roughly 7 spoons of Maggi
2-4 spoons of crushed pepper

and let it boil for 1 hour, and monitor, but it could be longer depending on how soft you want it

When the meat is soft enough

You add more water, depending on how thick or watery you want it to be, soup-wise
and add 1/2 teaspoon of:

4 spoons pepper soup seasoning
roughly 2-3 spoons of Maggi after till it tastes right, your call

let it simmer for 5-10 minutes, to cool off, and eat.

should be spicy but tasty

Enjoy!

